# CODEOWNERS: review gate on ProximityKit's walls, its label registry and its byte formats.
#
# Every path here is load-bearing for a guarantee, as in the Fernlet repository's CODEOWNERS. With
# branch protection's "Require review from Code Owners" enabled, no change to these paths can merge
# without the owner's explicit approval, so a wall cannot be weakened in a drive-by commit.
#
# Deliberately narrow: ordinary package code is not listed, so this gate cannot rot into a rubber
# stamp. If a path is added here, say in the PR why it is load-bearing. GitHub never reports a
# pattern that matches nothing, so Scripts/codeowners-scan.py does: every rule must resolve to a
# path, and the paths the walls rest on must keep their rules.
#
# The code arrives later with its git history from the Fernlet repository. Until Package.swift
# exists, the rules under Sources/ and Tests/ match nothing, and the scan holds them. The list
# follows that repository's plan and the walls its plan steps A1.1.13 to A1.1.15 move into the
# package's tests. Later steps there, A1.1.17 among them, move more walls in files not named yet:
# the commit that imports the code completes this list.

# The label registry: the host-supplied namespace and the domain-separation labels that every
# signature, seal and key derivation is bound to. Changing a label breaks the wire and on-disk
# formats of every app built on the package, and two namespaces sharing a label would let one
# app's bytes validate as another's. The namespace wall holds every namespace group and purpose
# construction to this folder. The same reasoning puts FernletCrypto/ under the owner in the
# Fernlet repository, and this rule mirrors that one.
/Sources/ProximityKit/Namespace/                                       @bowman-mw

# At-rest formats owned like FernletCrypto's originals: the mesh stores' V3 seal and its device binding.
/Sources/ProximityKit/Support/ProximityColumnCrypto.swift              @bowman-mw
/Sources/ProximityKit/Support/ProximityInstallBinding.swift            @bowman-mw
# The keychain funnel: every identity row's and seal key's query dictionary, the six calls that issue
# them, and the Debug-only backend door the tests install an in-memory store through.
/Sources/ProximityKit/Support/ProximityKeychainItem.swift              @bowman-mw
# The presence engine: the posture mint, the advertised record and self-exclusion by name.
/Sources/ProximityKit/Presence/ProximityPresenceSession.swift          @bowman-mw
# The identity's provisioning participant seam a host's escrow key rides.
/Sources/ProximityKit/Identity/IdentityProvisioningParticipant.swift   @bowman-mw

# The walls that travelled from the Fernlet repository (namespace, platform, keychain door), the
# presence engine's own cells, and the byte goldens the package holds.
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/ProximityNamespaceBoundaryTests.swift         @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/ProximityPlatformNeutralityTests.swift        @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/ProximityKeychainDoorTests.swift              @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/ProximityPresenceSessionTests.swift           @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/ProximityNamespaceSoundnessTests.swift        @bowman-mw

# The package tests' own walls: their hygiene (what their unhosted bundle cannot serve, their
# imports, their inventory, no extension of ProximityHost), the walls over the test tree, and the
# walls over ProximityKit's own sources.
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/PackageTestHygieneTests.swift                 @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/PackageTestTreeWallTests.swift                @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/ProximitySourceWallTests.swift                @bowman-mw
# The inventory of the package's tests: the hygiene suite holds it to the test tree, and it is the
# test-count floor's declared pin, held against the floor literals in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
/Tests/ProximityKitTests.tsv                                           @bowman-mw

# What every wall reads through (a blind lexer, locator or walker passes every wall vacuously), the
# installer (the audit sink and the in-memory keychain store) and the store it installs, and the
# test namespace the goldens compute under.
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/TestSupport/SwiftSourceLexer.swift            @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/TestSupport/PackageRoot.swift                 @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/TestSupport/PackageSwiftFiles.swift           @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/TestSupport/PackageTestEnvironment.swift      @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/TestSupport/PackageKeychainStore.swift        @bowman-mw
/Tests/ProximityKitTests/TestSupport/PackageTestNamespace.swift        @bowman-mw

# The manifest the namespace wall and the no-tracking wall pin (dependencies: [] both ways).
/Package.swift                                                         @bowman-mw

# The walls, their allowlist, and the CI that runs them (this file included). An allowlist entry is
# a sanctioned exception, so adding one deserves the same review as weakening a wall.
/Scripts/                                                              @bowman-mw
/.github/                                                              @bowman-mw
